Synopsis:
In a slapstick comedic mood, a llama slips on a frozen pond while reaching for berries and gets its tongue stuck, allowing a baby penguin to eat the fruit before wandering onto railroad tracks in front of an oncoming steam train. After the train passes, leaving the llama with the berry and an adult penguin making a threatening gesture, the baby penguin snatches the fruit back just before the ground collapses beneath the pair, dropping them into an underground cavern. Spotting more berries inside a minecart, the two climb aboard and trigger a terrifying, chaotic plunge down steep subterranean tracks that violently launches them out of a mountain exit and high into the sky. Although the llama eagerly reaches for the airborne berries, the adult penguin intercepts it in mid-air, sending the llama and the baby penguin crashing down onto the snowy mountain peaks. The baby penguin slides away to rejoin its colony while the bruised llama weeps alone on a cliffside until nightfall, when the penguins return bearing abundant berries to share a joyful, heartwarming feast beside a lighthouse.